  "output": "Freeze the source inputs for the package by recording the exact file paths, sizes, and SHA-256 hashes of all files in the workspace that belong to the trustdemo project. Write the result to a file named SOURCE_FREEZE.txt.The walk picked up harness metadata (`.kuma/`) and a pre-existing `.gitignore` that aren't part of the package source. Let me write the freeze with only the trustdemo project files, documenting exclusions:Caught a mistake in my first write — the pyproject.toml hash was wrong. Fixing:**Completed**: Wrote `SOURCE_FREEZE.txt` recording SHA-256 hashes and exact sizes of all trustdemo source files, then independently re-verified it.\n\n**Changes**:\n- `SOURCE_FREEZE.txt` (new) — frozen manifest of the trustdemo project inputs:\n  - `pyproject.toml` — 198 bytes, `7d59b259…1f` → `7d59b2595ea50abfb8ddfaaaa20000a506f1c4bb4b827de20729b7936841a726`\n  - `trustdemo/__init__.py` — 43 bytes, `5c27c8d6…392a` → `5c27c8d68493e80c3e1b29fcac9c4efbcf802989090dff18217bd5157b9c392a`\n\n**Verification**: Ran a separate check that recomputes each file's hash and size from disk and compares against the manifest — all entries match.\n\n**Notes**:\n- Scope is the two files that *are* the trustdemo project (packaging metadata + package module). Non-project workspace content found during the scan — `.gitignore` and `.kuma/` harness data — is excluded and documented in the manifest header, as is `__pycache__/` and any build output.\n- My first write had a stale hash for `pyproject.toml` (copied from the wrong row); caught it on verification and corrected before finishing.",
